    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1174">

                <pb facs="1184" n="898" xml:id="pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/136</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 20, 11.15 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>611. Just had audience with Sazonov which requested June 6 concerning Poland
                    relief. Delay caused by his absence. Declines passing on proposed plan before
                    conferring with Allies. Furthermore, positively objects to 150,000 soldiers or
                    anything near that number being maintained in Poland. Sent Dearing to Sazonov’s
                    assistant during Minister’s absence June 10, but was told Sazonov would pass on
                    question himself. Please advise Embassy further developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
